      en: "Apartadó is the most important commercial and urban center of the Urabá region in the Antioquia department. Its name comes from the indigenous language and means 'River of Bananas,' perfectly reflecting its role as the heart of Colombia's massive banana export industry. The city has experienced explosive growth in recent decades, transforming from a small settlement into a bustling modern city with major shopping malls and service centers. Apartadó serves as a hub for the surrounding banana and plantain plantations, which employ thousands of people and drive the local economy. Its population is a vibrant mix of people from across Colombia, creating a dynamic and multicultural urban environment near the Caribbean coast."
